## 5. User Profile Memory: Hierarchical Knowledge Graph Architecture

### 5.1 Design Motivation

Based on findings that:
1. Episodic memory provides both personalized knowledge and in-context learning benefits
2. Simply summarizing memory causes degradation in smaller models
3. Clearly providing personalized knowledge information enhances memory utilization

**Solution:** A hierarchical knowledge graph-based user profile memory module that manages personalized knowledge independently.

### 5.2 Three-Level Structure

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                         USER LEVEL                          │
│                    (user_0, user_1, ...)                   │
└─────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────┘
                          │ refers_to
                          ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                      KNOWLEDGE LEVEL                        │
│     Object Semantics          │        User Patterns        │
│   ("my coffee set")           │   ("my morning routine")    │
└──────────┬────────────────────┴──────────────┬──────────────┘
           │ composed_of                        │ entails
           ▼                                    ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                      ELEMENTS LEVEL                         │
│   Objects    │    Patterns    │    Locations                │
│ (red mug)    │   (place on)   │ (kitchen counter)          │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### 5.3 Node Schema

| Node Type | Attributes | Example |
|-----------|------------|---------|
| **User** | id, type, name | `{u1, "user", "james"}` |
| **Knowledge** | id, type, subtype, alias, description | `{k_obj1, "knowledge", "object_semantics", "my favorite cup", "a yellow cup with wooden handle"}` |
| **Pattern** | id, type, name, args | `{p1, "pattern", "place", [cup, on, livingroom_table]}` |
| **Object** | id, type, name, granularity | `{o2, "object", "red dog image cup", "instance"}` |
| **Location** | id, type, name, expression | `{l1, "location", "livingroom_table", "on the table"}` |

### 5.4 Edge Types

#### Hierarchical Edges (Structural Relationships)

| Source | Relation | Target |
|--------|----------|--------|
| User | refers_to | Knowledge |
| Knowledge | entails | Pattern |
| Pattern | target | Object |
| Pattern | target | Location |
| Knowledge | composed_of | Object |
| Knowledge | alias_of / target_object | Object |
| Knowledge | target_location | Location |

#### Temporal Edges (Sequential Ordering)

| Source | Relation | Target |
|--------|----------|--------|
| Pattern_n | before | Pattern_{n+1} |

**Purpose:** Encode sequential structure of user patterns (e.g., first pick cup, then place on table)

